course: dictionary
lesson: 3131
title: Same thing, different words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An elevator is a machine like a small room that carries people or things up and down between the floors of a building. In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, people call the same machine a lift. Both words are proper words for it.
explain: Use the words around a word to find its meaning. In «Take the elevator to the fifth floor», the clues are floor and up, so an elevator must be a machine that goes between floors. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence?
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A grain elevator is a tall building where farmers store grain, and a part on a plane's tail is also called an elevator. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is meant.
explain: Words change from place to place, but the thing stays the same. «Neither side is wrong» when people spell colour and color differently, and the same is true of lift and elevator. Safety clue: in a fire, use the stairs, not the elevator.
fact: An elevator is a machine that carries people or things up and down between floors.
fact: «Lift» means the same machine in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: A grain elevator is a tall building where farmers store grain.
fact: «British biscuit, pavement and lift are American cookie, sidewalk and elevator.»
fact: In a fire, use the stairs, not the elevator.
exercise: «Take the elevator to the fifth floor.» What is an elevator? | A small boat on a lake | A tall tree in a forest | *A machine that carries people up and down between floors | A type of biscuit
exercise: In a fire, which should you use to leave a tall building? | *The stairs | The roof | The elevator
exercise: What is a grain elevator? | *A tall building where farmers store grain | A part of a bicycle | A machine that carries grain up a hill | A small room in a house
test: In the UK, the machine that carries people between floors is called a what? | torch | pavement | queue | *lift
test: On a plane, the elevator is a part of the what? | engine | window | wing | *tail
exam: Ryan says «lift» and his American cousin says «elevator». What do both words mean? | A kind of biscuit | *A machine that carries people between floors | A tall building where farmers store grain | A part of a plane
